target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestStoreLinesAreRunlogsLines'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    the tail counts LINES, blank ones included, as deque(fh, maxlen=limit) does; dropping blank lines before the tail moves the window, so a run the Python sees inside the tail falls outside it here, for both readers at once now that they share this stage
--- old
				lines = append(lines, pyStrip(l))
--- new
				if pyStrip(l) != "" {
					lines = append(lines, pyStrip(l))
				}
